   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1:
1). # of trainings (disaggregation by type of capacity building) developed and delivered in the UNPRPD programme. (Disaggregated by topics)
2). # of participants (disaggregated by type of stakeholder) disaggregated by sex, disability, rural/urban participating in capacity building activities funded or provided by UNPRPD programmes
3). # of knowledge products (disaggregated by type of product /Thematic focus) developed, piloted and disseminated to the relevant stakeholders to inform inclusive practices
4). # of mechanisms to share and exchange learning and evidence to inform inclusive policies and systemsm(disaggregated by national/ regional/global mechanism).

Outcome 2:
1).  # of national regulatory frameworks and systems changes targeted by the UNPRPD program 
2) # of multi-stakeholder coordination mechanisms (disaggregated formal/informal) to support legislative policy and systems changes developed or strengthened
3). # Stakeholders involved in consultation and validation processes (disaggregation by stakeholder (GOV/ UN/OPDs/other)

Outcome 3:
1).# of adopted/ implemented COVID-19 inclusive response and recovery plans and frameworks containing systematic mainstreaming of persons with disabilities including the most marginalised
2) # of identified persons with disabilities including through their representative organizations participating in the State&#x2019;s formulation/implementation of COVID-19 policy responses</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2022">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Project proposal approved by the UNPRPD Secretariat 
- National Disability law 
- Practical guideline on Access to Legal Aid for Persons with Disabilities 
- Vocational training guideline for persons with disabilities 
- Draft Law on Access to Information 
- National and sub national disability machinery</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Finalise UNJP programme document 
- Organise LPAC meeting 
- Organise the 1st UNJP Steering Committee Meeting 
- Grant agreements with project partners
- Finalise the draft disability law 
- Review NDSP2, 2019-2023 and develop the new NDSP3, 2024-2029</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- The UNJP programme document finalised and approved by the UN participating agencies and the Royal Government of Cambodia. 
- The LPAC meeting was organised and endorsed on the UNJP named Accelerating Disability Rights in Cambodia (ADRC). 
- The first UNDP Steering Commitee Meeting was conducted and approved on the annual workplan 2022 as well as to endorse on the members of Steering Committee, the two Co-Chairs - Secretary of State of the Ministry of Social Affairs Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation (MoSVY) and UN Resident Coordinator, head of the three agencies are the members together with the representative of Ministry of Economic and Finance (MEF), representatives from persons with disabilities. 
- Two grant agreements were signed and kicked off its implementation. 
- The draft disability law was finalised and under the review of General Department of the Social Policy before submission to the Council of Minister for review and finalising it. 
- The NDSP 2 was reviewed and reflected the progress, challenges and lessons learnt identified. The recommendations were highlighted for the next NDSP 3.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
